diff --git a/changelog.d/7642-proximity-oracle-rows-no-call-path.md b/changelog.d/7642-proximity-oracle-rows-no-call-path.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..03a62b084
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/7642-proximity-oracle-rows-no-call-path.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+<!-- section: Fixed -->
+- On `exposed` and unknown-class findings, a matched oracle row whose related-test link is proximity-only (same file or module, name match, token substring, import-path or fixture affinity, seam-callee) now carries the `no_call_path` miss it always established, so the row renders as "misses: no call to the changed code found; linked by file location only" next to its oracle instead of reading as an unqualified discriminator. Rows with no recorded relation reason and rows without a matched oracle keep the unknown; no classification or reach decision reads the annotation (#7642).
+- The evidence-promotion-honesty corpus `expected_related_test` assertion accepts an optional `miss` pin (a known miss string, or explicit `null` to require no miss), and the `match_arm_proximity_wrapper_confirms` case pins the reaching row with no miss beside both proximity sibling rows carrying `no_call_path` (#7642).
diff --git a/changelog.d/7643-hidden-bullet-currentness.md b/changelog.d/7643-hidden-bullet-currentness.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..6a8ce153f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/7643-hidden-bullet-currentness.md
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+<!-- section: Fixed -->
+- In the `Hidden:` block, each omitted-finding bullet now appends its source-currentness category (`lower-priority candidate`, `base-side`, or `unresolved currentness`) whenever the omitted set mixes categories, so the count line's clauses connect to individual rows and a base-deleted evidence row is no longer mistaken for an outranked candidate at the same file:line. Single-category omitted sets keep the legacy unlabeled bullet, which the count line already names (#7643).
